<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong railways to defer fare adjustment.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong railways to defer fare adjustment.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's Kowloon-Canton Railway Corp and Mass Transit Railway Corp said they would defer their fare adjustments in May in order to tie in with the introduction of a new ticketing system planned for September.</p>
<p>The two government-owned corporations, which run the territory's above-ground and underground railway systems, said they will need to spend some time working out a new fare collection system for the planned Octopus smart card.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6441</p>
</text>
